  <UserdefinedSymbols />
  <Comments>Original implementation. DrummerIX reference CT was read for context only; addresses and machine instructions were independently checked in the running game. No third-party scripts are embedded. Enable parent first. All features require gameplay testing. Disable children before parent, and disable everything before closing Cheat Engine. Gil changes remain after disabling. SP options share hooks and can be combined. XP and level changes become visible after battle, when back on the field. User confirmed foundation scripts work in gameplay on 2026-10-10. User also confirmed v3 God Mode and Infinite Battle AP work. User confirmed v4 damage and max-vitals options work. One-Hit Kill overrides the player multiplier; God Mode and Always Max override the enemy multiplier. Multipliers operate by target side, not attacker identity. Healing and zero-damage hits are not multiplied. Enable Always Max in battle; if party actors are rebuilt, retoggle it to rediscover them. Always Max does not revive KO actors; refilled values remain after disabling. v5 adds zero ability AP costs and two shared-hook item consumption modes; gameplay testing needed. Infinite Usage overrides Never Below 1. Item routines may also serve non-use inventory removal; disable item options for selling, crafting, or quest hand-ins until tested. User confirmed v5 options work in gameplay. v6 adds Easy Imprism readiness and chance hooks for known enemy Mirage actors with a native capture capability. Native Prism, living-target, and other eligibility checks remain. No actor capture-state fields are edited. Boss/uncapturable bypass, capture replacement, and Champion-cost features are not implemented.</Comments>
</CheatTable>